Box64: keep the guest's PROT_EXEC when the host refuses it (Android noexec shared storage)

Android mounts /storage/emulated noexec. A game installed there has its DLLs mapped by Wine with
mmap/mprotect(PROT_EXEC), which the host refuses (EPERM/EACCES). Box64 records a page as executable
only after the host call succeeds, so it then refuses to run the guest code ("Emit Signal 11 ...
prot=3", Wine: access violation, execute). Box64 never runs guest pages natively, so retry without
host exec and record the guest's full protection. Only taken when the host call has failed.
Made against github.com/Pipetto-crypto/box64 at eb6fb21f (GameNative's Box64), after 0001.

